## Notes for the reviewer

- **Clarifications from the orchestrator, and where each is honoured.** (1) "Naming the field" is asserted as the error STRING containing the field key as a whole word (`names()` in test/event-fixtures.ts), never as a parenthesised suffix, and the non-object-body case asserts only a 400 and a non-empty string error; the one place a parenthesised suffix is plan-fixed (`(q)` in Task 7) is still matched by the same word-boundary check, so no wording is pinned. (2) The one-character `q` is tested for EVENTS only (400 naming `q`); nothing new is asserted about `GET /api/tasks`. (3) "Span" is the inclusive day count: 62 accepted and 63 refused for events, 31 accepted and 32 refused for the Google window. (4) The Google `from`/`to` tests are in a NEW file; test/task-list-contract.test.ts and the three shipped Google suites are untouched. (5) The export envelope/dump tests, the `.ics` tests and the stale comment are updated with ledger entries, never loosened. (6) Every route suite uses `isolatedIt as it` with `beforeEach(resetTaskTables, DRAIN_BUDGET_MS)`; no `resetEventTables` workaround. (7) No digest or golden value had to be computed this session: the one golden used is the phase-1 digest `c25b398c...6e79` (test/event-hash.test.ts), which is the digest of exactly the AC-9 payload (title `Dentista`, no description, location `Clínica Sorriso`, startAt 1792499400, endAt 1792503000, `America/Sao_Paulo`); its `startAt`/`endAt` literals are the same numbers. (8) vitest.config.ts was edited only to register the Node-side file in both projects.
- **What is pinned beyond the PRD's literal text, each justified by the plan** (so the reviewer can overrule any of them): the half-open edge cases of the range read (Task 7: an Event ending exactly at the range start is outside, a zero-duration Event at the start is inside and at the end is outside, a wrapping Event is inside, an all-day exclusive end never leaks), the range being read in the owner's zone whatever zone an Event was authored in (Task 7/15), the order tie-breaks (all-day first, then start, then id), POST's closed key set for `id` and `createdAt` (Task 6; AC-10 itself names only `source` and `contentHash`), the empty-body PATCH being 400 (Task 8), `title: null` on PATCH being 400 (Task 8), PATCH toggling both ways with only the target shape's fields (Task 8), a zero-duration Event omitting `DTEND` in the `.ics` (Task 13, RFC 5545), a refused Google window making no outbound call and being a 400 even with no connection (Task 10, deliberate), the `q`-only search cap and newest-first order (AC-17 text), and the docs rows' shape (Task 15). Deliberately NOT pinned: error wording, the order of search results when a range is present, a lone `from` or `to` together with `q`, a PATCH `{allDay: true}` with no `startDate`, and moving only `startAt` past the stored end.
- **Anti-vacuity.** The 401-gate suite is built around the fact that the gate answers 401 for any `/api/*` path, mounted or not; every case ends with a positive control. Unknown-id 404 cases carry a positive control. A delegated pre-flight found two cases that passed today only because they asserted no status (the google link case in test/event-routes-delete.test.ts and the "valid keys beside a refused one" case in test/event-routes-edit.test.ts); both now assert their 409 and 400 and were fixed before this manifest was finalised.
